<title>UK: UK's Bulmer buys Harvest for 2.4 mln NZD.</title>
<headline>UK's Bulmer buys Harvest for 2.4 mln NZD.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British cidermaker H.P. Bulmer Holdings Plc said on Monday that following clearance from New Zealand's monopolies panel it has bought Harvest Wine Company Ltd for 2.4 million New Zealand dollars.</p>
<p>New Zealand's Commerce Commission said last week that it had cleared Bulmer Trading (NZ) Ltd's proposed purchase of the cider making assets of Harvest Wine.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
